                    {
                        "sense_id": "75d56b0f-2c69-3680-93e6-ba8880ee3d0a",
                        "entry_id": "181e7fca-cf56-3941-ac79-3903ea5dcd3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "vorm van spot waarbij je het tegendeel zegt van wat je bedoelt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4830927-8c6e-4171-bfd1-0039f4cb451d",
                                "sense_id": "75d56b0f-2c69-3680-93e6-ba8880ee3d0a",
                                "text": "De verbitterde ironie van zijn zoon was niet te missen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67a483bc-fb27-3203-8620-40f5a94bc426",
                        "entry_id": "181e7fca-cf56-3941-ac79-3903ea5dcd3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "spottende uitlating waarbij je het tegendeel zegt van wat je bedoelt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39b089cc-5ad2-432e-987d-2df55eec70fb",
                                "sense_id": "67a483bc-fb27-3203-8620-40f5a94bc426",
                                "text": "Misschien is het waar dat je over alles wel ironisch kunt doen, maar het is ook onzin. Er zijn geen twee ironieën aan elkaar gelijk, ik bedoel, elke ironie heeft zijn eigen tint."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "495eb972-1ac6-3f06-a940-75a6aef7c608",
                        "entry_id": "181e7fca-cf56-3941-ac79-3903ea5dcd3e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "situatie die als je erover nadenkt het tegendeel laat zien van wat betoogd werd"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd735a4e-6b6b-43d2-8b86-d581ea9b5b31",
                                "sense_id": "495eb972-1ac6-3f06-a940-75a6aef7c608",
                                "text": "Na een heftige periode van drugs & drank kwam hij tot gezonde inkeer, totdat een kwaadaardig gezwel hem alsnog velde in '94. Wat een ironie dat de stand-up comedian in deze Relentless nog flink de draak steekt met gezonde joggers die op tofoe leven, terwijl hij zelf dikke sigarettenrookpluimen uit staat te blazen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "66cd48b7-988c-46e4-9066-80357b30a823",
                        "source_entry_id": "181e7fca-cf56-3941-ac79-3903ea5dcd3e",
                        "source_sense_id": "75d56b0f-2c69-3680-93e6-ba8880ee3d0a",
                        "source_sense_description": "vorm van spot",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ironie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ironie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5a0b370-1b98-3bd4-9d08-44e27a02c5ff",
                                        "entry_id": "4b14af29-bb4e-3ac6-ad40-c34aa5f41042",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "verhüllter Spott, bei dem ein Unterschied zwischen wörtlicher und wirklicher Bedeutung besteht"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce03b809-3e13-43ee-ab64-b0aaaf979d33",
                                                "sense_id": "b5a0b370-1b98-3bd4-9d08-44e27a02c5ff",
                                                "text": "Jemand erzählt einen schlechten Witz. Darauf reagiert eine andere Person mit Ironie: „Sehr witzig!“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9bb72b5-782a-40fc-ad32-3a3dab40bb70",
                                                "sense_id": "b5a0b370-1b98-3bd4-9d08-44e27a02c5ff",
                                                "text": "„In seinem Werk gibt es beides; zudem ist seine Ironie schwebend, so dass sie nicht einfach das Gegenteil des tatsächlich Gesagten meint.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93f4f6c4-da8c-45fa-911d-f99fa4ece47b",
                                                "sense_id": "b5a0b370-1b98-3bd4-9d08-44e27a02c5ff",
                                                "text": "„Die Ironie der Novelle liegt weniger in der Sprechweise als in der Situation des Erzählers.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc483475-54b1-45d6-a9d3-fb47b1cdc4a8",
                                                "sense_id": "b5a0b370-1b98-3bd4-9d08-44e27a02c5ff",
                                                "text": "„Vor den Fotoseiten hockend, verlor ich all meine angesammelte Spottlust, meine allzeit bereite Ironie, meine schnelle Frechheit.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "991d7358-269d-41fe-9ec2-75819cb3996c",
                                                "sense_id": "b5a0b370-1b98-3bd4-9d08-44e27a02c5ff",
                                                "text": "„Das sollte ironisch klingen, so wie eben ein fast siebzigjähriger Vater mit seinem voll erwachsenen Sohn spricht, aber die Ironie gelang ihm nicht, sie fror an dem Wort Geld fest.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c44e4645-4dea-44ea-8145-133d2253b7f5",
                        "source_entry_id": "181e7fca-cf56-3941-ac79-3903ea5dcd3e",
                        "source_sense_id": "75d56b0f-2c69-3680-93e6-ba8880ee3d0a",
                        "source_sense_description": "vorm van spot",
                        "target_lang_word": "irony",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "irony",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e1efacb-27d2-37b2-a6aa-98be5437693e",
                                        "entry_id": "b9db7755-5c43-39c1-a84b-bf82e37babf5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of a statement that, when taken in context, may actually mean something different from, or the opposite of, what is written literally; the use of words expressing something other than their literal intention, often in a humorous context."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6998bb7-0de8-4a76-b500-af8a686372e2",
                                                "sense_id": "5e1efacb-27d2-37b2-a6aa-98be5437693e",
                                                "text": "Irony, saying what it ne'er intends,\nCensures with praise, and speaks to foes as friends."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9cb1998-5e79-4fd3-aa8b-9a68e96e2b2f",
                                                "sense_id": "5e1efacb-27d2-37b2-a6aa-98be5437693e",
                                                "text": "A principal virtue of Rorty's recognition of both the lightminded and the serious side of irony is to urge us in that direction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c17c2a7f-21dc-34d1-905e-bad79a13945f",
                                        "entry_id": "b9db7755-5c43-39c1-a84b-bf82e37babf5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of a statement that, when taken in context, may actually mean something different from, or the opposite of, what is written literally; the use of words expressing something other than their literal intention, often in a humorous context.",
                                            "An ironic statement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce9621ba-e13c-4eac-9bea-878ec6a8b64a",
                                                "sense_id": "c17c2a7f-21dc-34d1-905e-bad79a13945f",
                                                "text": "It is one of the ironies of capital cities that each acts as a symbol of its nation, and yet few are even remotely representative of it. London has always set itself apart from the rest of Britain — but political, economic and social trends are conspiring to drive that wedge deeper."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7e8b25d-c62d-41f2-a0a8-c5c23b915293",
                                                "sense_id": "c17c2a7f-21dc-34d1-905e-bad79a13945f",
                                                "text": "The second irony is that the only American who intuitively or otherwise grasps this reality and possesses a large enough ego potentially capable of governing in these circumstances is the president."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e6226bc-3a5f-308f-91a9-6c8e66b31f8c",
                                        "entry_id": "b9db7755-5c43-39c1-a84b-bf82e37babf5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dramatic irony: a theatrical effect in which the meaning of a situation, or some incongruity in the plot, is understood by the audience, but not by the characters in the play."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbdd0a07-bb3e-302c-abc5-2b2fe3533982",
                                        "entry_id": "b9db7755-5c43-39c1-a84b-bf82e37babf5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Socratic irony: ignorance feigned for the purpose of confounding or provoking an antagonist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14306e07-2652-3f53-a401-74f35277765a",
                                        "entry_id": "b9db7755-5c43-39c1-a84b-bf82e37babf5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Contradiction between circumstances and expectations; condition contrary to what might be expected."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "informal",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "irony",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                        "entry_id": "ac8b4d32-dd7d-3a9e-83df-225a845e9d4a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to the metal iron."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e4c2b61-cc14-43fe-aad6-a23bb1b521e7",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "The food had an irony taste to it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44d3a61d-58ea-421d-ac11-54f514ce8700",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "The scrap yard had bins marked for irony aluminum, such as aluminum engine blocks not wholly cleaned of bolts, studs, brackets, and so on."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0b06e2c-e9c6-4816-8140-19caede3cbcc",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "Thus in Cornwall, and many parts of Germany and France, in mineral districts, an irony appearance of a vein, where seen at the crop, is regarded as favourable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8272ff7-efd7-409c-ae0a-2b948ca76dca",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "E. W. Baker, Main St. - No odor, good appearance, slight irony taste; pressure weak. But water which had stood in wash pitcher some three or four days showed pronounced odor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fead968c-948c-4c79-b8e5-126c13ced03e",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "There can be no doubt that persistent biking robs the female limb of its graceful contour and substitutes therefore the rugged protrusive muscles, the ungainly and irony look of the masculine leg."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23304d30-6292-43ea-88ed-56220eeb98ef",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "It [overgrazing] eventually causes a particularly hard irony surface to the soil which is perfectly unmistakable once you have seen it , and also certain weeds which are also unmistakable once you have seen them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af58a486-3634-460b-8e31-b5dc93d86308",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "Raspberries raw, stewing, jamming, pulping, take over my house during July, overlaying the richer, more irony smell of the blackcurrant – a contralto to a soprano."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "706b4ebf-ae28-4ea0-be4e-8342261f7f79",
                                                "sense_id": "7f3506c4-cb4e-3cfa-b425-8baf39154f17",
                                                "text": "There was nothing left, besides just the pile of files on my desk, and the irony look on Catherine's face."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "irony",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "457d0e92-9d3c-3cf6-99c1-dd251165e02b",
                                        "entry_id": "374f64bf-a77f-3caf-a1e8-2539ff92d376",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kind of metallic marble."
